                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 187,
                "quote": "if (ports.Files.ReadLines path).IsSome then"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 178,
                "quote": "with _ ->\n            None"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "All new effects go through existing ports: Archive.Load/Save, Files.ReadLines and Store.Load/Save. Nothing new is done in Tier 1/2. The change also fixes an existing violation: presentation used to call `JsonFileStore.create path` directly (an ARC-BND-01 bypass), and it now calls UseCases.backup. One finding is reported but does not fail the check: loadBackup has a catch-all handler in Tier 3 that does not re-raise (ARC-HEU-01). It turns any archive failure, such as a corrupt or unreadable file, into 'no backup' instead of keeping it as an explicit outcome. This does not meet any level-1 condition of the rubric, so the score stays 2.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 324,
                "quote": "let summary (library: Library) : SummaryView ="
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The library summary is defined once (Views.summary) and used by backup, restore and backup-info. Its text is rendered once (showSummary). The amount owed comes from the existing Accounts.owed, and money formatting reuses Views.money. No literal or predicate is copied.",
            "score": 2
          }
        },
